# 10. AGENT-TO-AGENT COMMUNICATION

Do NOT allow unrestricted direct agent-to-agent communication.

Introduce controlled coordination messages.

A message should include:

* message ID
* coordination ID
* sender agent
* recipient agent
* message type
* payload
* timestamp
* correlation metadata
* schema/version

Messages must be:

* bounded
* validated
* authorized
* sanitized
* observable

The coordinator remains the authority.

Agents should not secretly invoke other agents.

