# 20. SECURITY / PROMPT-INJECTION DEFENSE

Treat every agent result and inter-agent message as potentially untrusted.

Never interpret agent output as privileged system instructions.

Use the same security principles already implemented in Sprint 17/18:

* bounded input
* schema validation
* delimiter/boundary handling
* secret redaction
* connection-string protection
* output size limits
* metadata allowlisting
* no credential forwarding
* no arbitrary code execution
* no hidden tool expansion

Agent output must remain data.

